<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3840" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aruns</span></b> , untis, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an Etruscan name of</i>
			
			<i>the younger son</i>, while the elder was called Lar
			or Lars [in pure Etruscan, Arnth.; Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρρων</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρροῦνς</span>]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A brother of Lucumo</i> (Tarquinius Priscus), <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
			34</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A younger son of Tarquin the Proud</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
			56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2,
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A son of Porsenna</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 2,
			14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>An Etruscan seer</i>, <i><span class="en">Luc. 1,
			585</span></i>; v. Müll. Etrusk. 1, pp. 405 and 409.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
